diff --git a/fleet-patches/0003-common-guard-checkpoint-update_dft-against-an-empty-.patch b/fleet-patches/0003-common-guard-checkpoint-update_dft-against-an-empty-.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..69fe82a6a1
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fleet-patches/0003-common-guard-checkpoint-update_dft-against-an-empty-.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,106 @@
+From d77152d47816bd077386890d31ec309c1a78ae18 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Doug Gabehart <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 20:53:47 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] common: guard checkpoint update_dft against an empty draft
+ sequence
+
+SIGSEGV / GGML_ASSERT("tensor not allocated") crash in create_checkpoint
+-> update_dft, taking down the whole llama-server process, under
+`--parallel>1` + draft-mtp (or any speculative type). Found live while
+root-causing a --parallel N-slot collapse rollout crash.
+
+REPRODUCTION: single request, no concurrent traffic, long prompt (>16K
+tokens, crossing the second `checkpoint_min_step` boundary at
+2*8192=16384) sent to a fresh, previously-idle slot under `--parallel 3`.
+Crashed mid PROMPT PROCESSING (prefill), before any token generation
+began:
+
+  I slot print_timing: id  2 | task 0 | prompt processing, n_tokens = 16477
+  D slot   operator(): id  2 | task 0 | main/do_checkpoint = yes, pos_min = 16476, pos_max = 16476
+  /app/ggml/src/ggml-backend.cpp:359: GGML_ASSERT(tensor->data != NULL && "tensor not allocated") failed
+  ... state_seq_get_data -> common_prompt_checkpoint::update_dft -> create_checkpoint ...
+
+ROOT CAUSE: create_checkpoint() (tools/server/server-context.cpp)
+unconditionally calls common_prompt_checkpoint::update_dft(ctx_dft,
+slot.id, ...) whenever a checkpoint is created -- including one triggered
+by the periodic checkpoint_min_step threshold during PURE PROMPT PREFILL,
+before the draft/speculative model has ever performed a forward pass for
+that slot's sequence (draft-mtp, like every speculative type, only runs
+during token generation, never during prefill). update_dft then calls
+llama_state_seq_get_data_ext on ctx_dft for that sequence unconditionally.
+
+Under a UNIFIED KV cache (kv_unified = true, what --parallel 1 produces),
+the single shared backing buffer is fully allocated at context-creation
+time regardless of write history, so reading an as-yet-unused sequence's
+(empty but allocated) region never crashes.
+
+Under a SPLIT (non-unified) KV cache (kv_unified = false, what
+--parallel>1 produces on a hybrid/linear-attention architecture like
+Qwen3.8-27B / qwen3_5), each sequence's backing buffer is allocated
+lazily, only once that sequence is actually used. A sequence that has
+done real target-model prefill but has NEVER been touched by the DRAFT
+model specifically (exactly the mid-prefill-checkpoint case above) has a
+genuinely unallocated draft-context KV buffer for that seq_id. Reading it
+via llama_io_write_host inside state_seq_get_data hits ggml-backend's own
+tensor->data != NULL assert and aborts the whole process -- taking down
+every other slot's in-flight work too, not just the one request that
+triggered it.
+
+Note: this is a distinct bug from the ggml allocator's view-init issue
+(see the following commit) -- this one is a real empty/never-touched
+sequence being read at all; that one is a sequence whose backing view was
+never initialized even though it had been used.
+
+FIX: guard update_dft with llama_memory_seq_pos_max(ctx_dft, seq_id) < 0
+(the documented upstream API for "this sequence is empty in this
+memory") immediately after the existing ctx == nullptr early-return. When
+the draft context genuinely has nothing for this sequence yet, leave
+data_dft empty and return -- exactly the same state already produced
+today when speculative decoding is disabled entirely (ctx_dft ==
+nullptr). common_prompt_checkpoint::load_dft already no-ops on an empty
+data_dft, so restoring a checkpoint created in this state correctly skips
+restoring draft state that never existed, rather than erroring.
+
+No upstream PR tracks this -- original work, not a vendored port. This
+looks like a genuine, previously-unreported bug affecting anyone running
+speculative decoding with --parallel>1 on a split/non-unified KV cache,
+worth filing upstream separately.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017R3QNP4GznFWhhf11QY18j
+(cherry picked from commit 6fcd12020b678a84facfed47ff516fa22d9cb3a5)
+---
+ common/common.cpp | 17 +++++++++++++++++
+ 1 file changed, 17 insertions(+)
+
+diff --git a/common/common.cpp b/common/common.cpp
+index e36f8ab502..163fae56fa 100644
+--- a/common/common.cpp
++++ b/common/common.cpp
+@@ -2373,6 +2373,23 @@ void common_prompt_checkpoint::update_dft(
+         return;
+     }
+ 
++    // a checkpoint can be created while still in the prompt-prefill phase of
++    // a request (see create_checkpoint()'s periodic min-step trigger in
++    // tools/server/server-context.cpp), before the draft/speculative model
++    // has ever run a forward pass for this sequence -- draft-mtp and other
++    // speculative types only decode during token generation, not prefill.
++    // Under a split (non-unified) KV cache -- forced by --parallel>1 on
++    // hybrid/recurrent-layer architectures -- an unused sequence's backing
++    // buffer is not yet allocated, so reading it here would hit an
++    // unallocated tensor and hard-abort the whole process. Treat "nothing
++    // decoded yet" the same as "no draft context at all" (ctx == nullptr
++    // above): data_dft stays empty, and load_dft() already no-ops on an
++    // empty data_dft.
++    if (llama_memory_seq_pos_max(llama_get_memory(ctx), seq_id) < 0) {
++        data_dft.clear();
++        return;
++    }
++
+     const size_t ckpt_size = llama_state_seq_get_size_ext(ctx, seq_id, flags);
+ 
+     data_dft.resize(ckpt_size);
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
diff --git a/fleet-patches/0004-ci-add-sync-with-upstream-workflow-mirror-of-the-mas.patch b/fleet-patches/0004-ci-add-sync-with-upstream-workflow-mirror-of-the-mas.patch
new file mode 100644
index 0000000000..6ff82b8e6d
--- /dev/null
+++ b/fleet-patches/0004-ci-add-sync-with-upstream-workflow-mirror-of-the-mas.patch
@@ -0,0 +1,132 @@
+From 805a228964449be21baa874d59a630a3564b83d4 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: Doug Gabehart <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 9 Sep 2026 20:59:11 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] ci: add sync-with-upstream workflow (mirror of the master
+ copy)
+
+Same file as master's .github/workflows/sync-fleet-patches.yml -- present
+here too so workflow_dispatch can target this branch directly and its
+content stays visible alongside the commits it operates on. The
+schedule trigger itself only ever fires from master's copy (GitHub
+requirement); this copy is for manual dispatch and documentation
+purposes.
+
+Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
+Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_017R3QNP4GznFWhhf11QY18j
+(cherry picked from commit 9f9044d3899f5e33f5cc807b0f226df0b64e6fff)
+---
+ .github/workflows/sync-fleet-patches.yml | 102 +++++++++++++++++++++++
+ 1 file changed, 102 insertions(+)
+ create mode 100644 .github/workflows/sync-fleet-patches.yml
+
+diff --git a/.github/workflows/sync-fleet-patches.yml b/.github/workflows/sync-fleet-patches.yml
+new file mode 100644
+index 0000000000..258a40b59e
+--- /dev/null
++++ b/.github/workflows/sync-fleet-patches.yml
+@@ -0,0 +1,102 @@
++name: Sync fleet-patches with upstream
++
++# Keeps the `fleet-patches` branch (home-infrastructure's llamacpp-rpc image
++# build source, see deployments/llamacpp-rpc/image/Dockerfile's LLAMACPP_REF
++# header comment there) rebased on top of ggml-org/llama.cpp master. This
++# replaces the old workflow of manually re-checking `git apply --check`
++# against a new pin and hand-editing patch files -- a clean rebase here IS
++# that re-verification, done by git itself.
++#
++# - Clean rebase: force-pushed automatically. The branch always ends up as
++#   "current upstream master + our 4 patch commits", nothing more.
++# - Conflicting rebase: aborted, branch left untouched at its last-known-good
++#   state, and a single tracking issue is opened (or left alone if one is
++#   already open) describing the conflict for manual resolution.
++#
++# Bumping home-infrastructure's Dockerfile LLAMACPP_REF pin to a newer
++# fleet-patches commit after a sync stays a separate, deliberate step in
++# that repo (same re-verification discipline as any other pin bump) -- this
++# workflow never touches anything outside this repo.
++
++on:
++  schedule:
++    # Weekly, Monday 06:00 UTC. Scheduled workflows are disabled by default
++    # on GitHub for a repo with no recent activity -- re-enable under this
++    # repo's Actions tab if it ever goes quiet and this stops firing.
++    - cron: "0 6 * * 1"
++  workflow_dispatch: {}
++
++permissions:
++  contents: write
++  issues: write
++
++jobs:
++  sync:
++    runs-on: ubuntu-latest
++    steps:
++      - name: Checkout fleet-patches (full history)
++        uses: actions/checkout@v4
++        with:
++          ref: fleet-patches
++          fetch-depth: 0
++          persist-credentials: true
++
++      - name: Configure git identity
++        run: |
++          git config user.name "fleet-patches sync bot"
++          git config user.email "actions@users.noreply.github.com"
++
++      - name: Add upstream remote and fetch
++        run: |
++          git remote add upstream https://github.com/ggml-org/llama.cpp.git
++          git fetch upstream master
++
++      - name: Attempt rebase onto upstream/master
++        id: rebase
++        run: |
++          set +e
++          git rebase upstream/master
++          status=$?
++          set -e
++          if [ "$status" -ne 0 ]; then
++            git rebase --abort
++            echo "conflict=true" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
++          else
++            echo "conflict=false" >> "$GITHUB_OUTPUT"
++          fi
++
++      - name: Push rebased branch
++        if: steps.rebase.outputs.conflict == 'false'
++        run: |
++          # Compare against the pre-rebase remote tip so a fully-up-to-date
++          # branch (nothing to rebase) is a silent no-op, not a force-push.
++          before="$(git rev-parse origin/fleet-patches)"
++          after="$(git rev-parse HEAD)"
++          if [ "$before" = "$after" ]; then
++            echo "Already up to date with upstream/master -- nothing to push."
++          else
++            git push --force-with-lease origin fleet-patches:fleet-patches
++            echo "Pushed rebased fleet-patches: $before -> $after"
++          fi
++
++      - name: Open or update conflict tracking issue
++        if: steps.rebase.outputs.conflict == 'true'
++        env:
++          GH_TOKEN: ${{ github.token }}
++        run: |
++          existing="$(gh issue list --repo "$GITHUB_REPOSITORY" \
++            --search 'in:title "fleet-patches rebase conflict"' \
++            --state open --json number --jq '.[0].number')"
++          upstream_sha="$(git rev-parse upstream/master)"
++          if [ -n "$existing" ]; then
++            gh issue comment "$existing" --repo "$GITHUB_REPOSITORY" \
++              --body "Still conflicting as of upstream master \`$upstream_sha\` ($(date -u +%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%SZ)). fleet-patches was left untouched at its last-known-good commit."
++          else
++            gh issue create --repo "$GITHUB_REPOSITORY" \
++              --title "fleet-patches rebase conflict against upstream master" \
++              --body "The scheduled sync workflow could not cleanly rebase \`fleet-patches\` onto \`upstream/master\` (\`$upstream_sha\`). The branch has been left untouched at its last-known-good commit -- no broken state was pushed.
++
++Manual resolution needed: fetch this repo, \`git rebase upstream/master\` on \`fleet-patches\` locally, resolve conflicts, force-push. See each patch commit's own message for the rationale behind that specific change, to help judge how to resolve a conflict in it.
++
++Close this issue once resolved and pushed."
++          fi
+-- 
+2.43.0
+
