+- -ncmoe on a dense model adds patterns that match no tensor; only overrides
+  that match a tensor of the model keep the memory split, and that check
+  runs after the device count, so single-device runs log nothing
+- cached timings must be finite and positive, otherwise they are measured
+  again; an RPC entry is re-checked with a short (~32 MiB) decode timing and
+  measured again when the device behind the endpoint runs at other than
+  0.67-1.5x its cached speed
+- entries of other builds and expired ones are pruned on write, a failed
+  write is logged
+- predicted prefill/decode include the non-matmul time measured on
+  Qwen3.8-27B (x1.28 / x1.13)
