+From 3d4d1bc31d4f23a7f61d733f60848293d29e2bd3 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+Date: Thu, 24 Sep 2026 20:37:55 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] server: capture checkpoints in-batch only across devices,
+ read them after the next decode
+
+- in-batch capture pays off only when the model is split across devices (it
+  avoids draining that pipeline); on one device the batch split costs
+  nothing and the cut leaves shorter ubatches: Qwen3.8-27B on one GPU with
+  -b/-ub 1024 --parallel 3 lost 12-15% prompt speed (the gabesrv10 router
+  regression). LLAMA_SERVER_CKPT_CAPTURE=1 still forces it on
+- a capture is read after a later llama_decode() has been submitted (or
+  before the next task, or when nothing is left to decode), so reading it
+  no longer waits for the whole batch; the checkpoint decisions use what
+  was known when its batch was submitted
+
+Slot saves stay byte-identical to the split path (Qwen3.5-4B, 4 turns
+including a checkpoint restore).
+
+Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
+(cherry picked from commit 54920cfed550288441a1a544ca8a6b7724ebe676)
+---
+ tools/server/server-context.cpp | 100 +++++++++++++++++++++++++-------
+ 1 file changed, 78 insertions(+), 22 deletions(-)
+
