+Subject: [PATCH] common : split-balance: survive malformed cache entries, log
+ why an entry is not used, merge on write
+
+Fleet QA round 6 (Dawn):
+- One entry with a string measured_at made the cache prune throw after every
+  calibration, i.e. every start aborted; with the chart's persistent hostPath
+  cache that is a crashloop until someone deletes the file. Malformed entries
+  are now dropped.
+- An entry failing the decode/check consistency bound (4x) was rejected
+  without a log line, so every start recalibrated silently and busy detection
+  never ran. CPU rpc workers with MXFP4 measure 5.2x legitimately; the bound
+  is 16x now, and a rejected entry or reference logs why.
+- Two servers sharing a cache dir overwrote each other's entries. The write
+  now re-reads the file and merges this run's entries into it.
+
+test-split-balance starts from a file with a malformed entry.
+
+Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
+(cherry picked from commit d93fef38ae89f8c38aea6b7f8e31c1e1a1556848)
+---
