+From d1ed6605df0fb7c7bef2109bd794c247a65053b8 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
+From: dgabehar <dgabehar@gmail.com>
+Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 09:41:52 -0500
+Subject: [PATCH] sampling: K2-Horizon: Kimi hold gets its own small cap and
+ releases on a repeated opener
+
+Live 2026-09-29: with the EOG hold a K2 session looped ~1500 tokens of
+"<|tool_calls_section_begin|><|tool_call_begin|>" (blank lines between repeats) before
+ending. The Kimi hold now has k_kimi_hold_cap = 192 tokens (117 complete Kimi calls in
+the harness: median 42, longest 115) while the native hold keeps 2048, and an opener
+repeated while the first is unfinished releases EOG immediately. Switching to the native
+opener hands over to the native hold. The real loop text is a test fixture (8 checks fail
+against the previous guard). Release only permits EOG; it does not force the model to end.
+Forced-opener harness (40 samples): before 36 native / 4 loops to 2600 tokens, after 34
+native / 6 non-native, 5 still run to 2600 tokens because the model never picks EOG.
+ctest -L main 59/59, -R split-balance pass.
+
